    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d996">

                <pb facs="1155" n="959" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg959"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/7–2745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 996<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chief of the Division of
                        Economic Security Controls</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Oliver</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Director of the Office of Financial and Development Policy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Collado</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">and the Chief of the
                        Division of Economic Security Controls</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Rubin</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d996-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-27">July 27 [1945.]</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>148. For Collado and Rubin from Oliver.</p>
                <p>There follow as promised Fletcher’s
                    revised estimates on total German assets in neutrals. Figures in parentheses
                    represent April 30 estimates of overall report. All figures in millions dollars.
                    Switzerland 600 (300); this figure represents direct investments only. Portugal
                    35 (27). Sweden 51 (57.7). Turkey 51.2 (33). Spanish estimates not yet
                    reconciled.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d996-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d996-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Secretary of State at Babelsberg over the signature of Grew.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
